// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SimmonsDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page TaskIncomplete Text :
"P2172712231" "Are... Are you here to kill me?"
// Answer Text :
"P1551210925" "Kill you? No, I'm here to protect you..."
// Page Page1 Text :
"P618973148" "What? Then why did you just knock out my entire security detail?"
// Answer Text :
"P322796647" "Security? Those were Family goons, ma'am."
// Page Page2 Text :
"P1327839108" "Why, yes, Sebastian Frost did provide me with some of his boys for security, but it wasn't anything illegal.<br><br>The Skulls are targetting city officials that are putting our feet down to combat their Superadine dealing. Mr. Frost simple shares my point of view on the problem."
// Page Page2 SayOutLoudText :
"P853327526" "Why, yes, Sebastian Frost did provide me with some of his boys for security, but it wasn't anything illegal.<t 5>The Skulls are targetting city officials that are putting our feet down to combat their Superadine dealing.<t 6>Mr. Frost simple shares my point of view on the problem.<t 0.1>"
// Answer Text :
"P2535716893" "Wait, the Family wants to stomp out Superadine in Kings Row?"
// Page Page3 Text :
"P3661612175" "<color orange>Councilwoman Simmons appears to be ready to comment on that when she pauses suddenly and looks around nervously.</color><br><br>Do you feel that?"
// Page Page3 SayOutLoudText :
"P994537628" "Do you feel that?"
// Answer Text :
"P978906580" "Feel what?"
// Page TaskComplete Text :
"P69011690" "Please... You have to protect me!"
// Page MoranaDefeated Text :
"P5968590" "I... I don't know what to say..."
// Answer Text :
"P1034194438" "Start at the beginning."
// Page MoranaDefeatedPage1 Text :
"P416345397" "Frost came to me with a very sensible proposal. He wanted to clear his family name of the stain his father had put on it all those years ago. The link between his family and the street drug called Superadine.<br><br>I... I wanted to believe that he was doing it for the good of Paragon City, but deep down I knew he wasn't."
// Page MoranaDefeatedPage1 SayOutLoudText :
"P2412079494" "Frost came to me with a very sensible proposal.<t 3>He wanted to clear his family name of the stain his father had put on it all those years ago.<t 5>The link between his family and the street drug called Superadine.<t 5>I... I wanted to believe that he was doing it for the good of Paragon City, but deep down I knew he wasn't.<t 0.1>"
// Answer Text :
"P3920113802" "Keep going."
// Page MoranaDefeatedPage2 Text :
"P1871143426" "I empathized with him. I understand the difficulty that a parent's decisions can have on their children...<br><br><color orange>Councilwoman Simmons grows upset and wipes at the corner of her eye</color>"
// Page MoranaDefeatedPage2 SayOutLoudText :
"P300939116" "He told me that he knows what it's like to grow up without a parent...<t 0.1>"
// Answer Text :
"P2972359024" "It's ok, you can talk about it."
// Page MoranaDefeatedPage3 Text :
"P2487596259" "It's my husband, Carl. You see, he's very ill and to be honest... I'm not sure how much longer he has.<br><br>We've been keeping it a secret because, well, his illness was caused by his drug addiction. If the press were to learn of this, it would ruin our careers.<br><br>But worst of all, our son, Albert, would have to live with our failures hanging over him like a shadow, just like Sebastian Frost has had to live with his father's mistakes. I just wanted to find a way out.<br><br>Frost said that he would be willing to have some specialists come in to see what they could do for Carl, but only if I helped him. Standing up against Superadine seemed to be a suitably appropriate favor given the situation, I thought it was a sign that good things were to come...<br><br>I... I know it was a bribe, but... I was thinking of my family..."
// Page MoranaDefeatedPage3 SayOutLoudText :
"P683360885" "It's my husband, Carl.<t 3>You see, he's very ill and to be honest... I'm not sure how much longer he has.<t 5>We've been keeping it a secret because, well, his illness was caused by his drug addiction.<t 5>If the press were to learn of this, it would ruin our careers.<t 5>But worst of all, our son, Albert, would have to live with our failures hanging over him like a shadow, just like Sebastian Frost has had to live with his father's mistakes.<t 5>I just wanted to find a way out.<t 5>Frost said that he would be willing to have some specialists come in to see what they could do for Carl, but only if I helped him.<t 5>Standing up against Superadine seemed to be a suitably appropriate favor given the situation.<t 5>I thought it was a sign that good things were to come...<t 5>I... I know it was a bribe, but... I was thinking of my family...<t 0.1>"
// Answer Text :
"P214754606" "I understand, your secret is safe with me."
// Answer Text :
"P264241016" "I'm going to have to put you under arrest, Councilwoman."
// Page PageThankYou Text :
"P2422693539" "I see now that Sebastian Frost has just been using my position in the city council, and the position of others like John Hammett, to further his own ends. While I'll still stand up against Superadine, I will refuse Mr. Frost's offer.<br><br>Thank you for giving me a second chance."
// Page PageThankYou SayOutLoudText :
"P867649644" "I see now that Sebastian Frost has just been using my position in the city council, and the position of others like John Hammett, to further his own ends.<t 5>While I'll still stand up against Superadine, I will refuse Mr. Frost's offer.<t 3>Thank you for giving me a second chance.<t 0.1>"
// Answer Text :
"P967292869" "This city needs people like you with a good heart, one mistake doesn't make you a villain."
// Page PageArrest Text :
"P3807966046" "I... I understand. What I've done is a crime and I should face a jury of my peers.<br><br>I... I want to thank you for what you did today, {HeroName}... I just don't know what the future holds in store for us when the only ones who will stand up against The Skulls and street drugs like Superadine are the Frost Family."
// Page PageArrest SayOutLoudText :
"P1980347991" "I... I understand.<t 2>What I've done is a crime and I should face a jury of my peers.<t 5>I... I want to thank you for what you did today, {HeroName}...<t 3>I just don't know what the future holds in store for us when the only ones who will stand up against The Skulls and street drugs like Superadine are the Frost Family.<t 0.1>"
// Answer Text :
"P1594459811" "I'll stand up against them, now let's go."
// Page NotTaskOwner Text :
"P249727203" "<color orange>Only the task owner can speak with Councilwoman Simmons.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2118830492" "Listen, I have some old contacts that keep tabs on the goings on inside the Family. I'll talk with them and see what they know about the Family's presence here in Kings Row. This is way outside of their normal turf.<br><br>In the meantime, I've narrowed down the most likely target for the next assassination attempt by Veles' assassin. Councilwoman Simmons just finished a press conference demonizing The Skulls for their assassination of Councilman Hammett, and now she's vowed to take up Hammett's work and make sure The Skulls are brought to justice for their crimes against Paragon City and the citizens of Kings Row.<br><br>It's like she's painting a bull's eye on her own forehead."
// AcceptString :
"P2119182486" "I'll get over to Simmons' office right away"
// SendOffString :
"P1796799399" "One last thing, watch your back, {HeroName}.<br><br>The more I think about this situation the worse feeling I get. This whole things stinks of The Family trying to pave the way to keep The Skulls in business.<br><br>Ever since Sebastian Frost took over the family business from his late old man, the Family's taken great pains to appear hands off when it comes to Superadine.<br><br>Just... be careful, I don't want to see you end up like Mina...<br><br><color yellow>This mission is of higher difficulty than normal, you may want to bring a teammate.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1032809712" "Run security for Councilwoman Simmons"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1053240436" "Mina? Oh, yeah, Mina Horne. She was a Regulator, just like me, went by the name <color yellow>The Illustrated Woman</color>. Harry Frost's goons killed her in an ambush one night while we were on patrol. A retaliation attack for Harry's incarceration after we busted him with Superadine.<br><br><color orange>Eagle Eye takes a moment before continuing. This is obviously difficult for him.</color><br><br>I was running operations the night she was killed. I used to always tell her to watch her back before she went out on patrol without me...<br><br><color orange>Eagle Eye smirks at a fond memory before continuing.</color><br><br>She always used to say, 'I don't have to, you're watching it for me.' That night, though, I didn't say it to her. I don't know why I didn't, but I distinctly remember being uneasy about not telling her. Then I heard Michael over the radio saying Mina was hit...<br><br>I'm sorry, it's just... {HeroName}, watch your back."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4043635011" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Deadly Little Girl</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3947020704" "The Family has goons all over this building. Have you arrived too late?"
